    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I was born with a rare eye disease called Leber’s Congenital Amaurosis. Because of it, my eyesight is very poor. I can sense light and detect objects in front of me, but that’s about it. The disease also makes my eyes "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "extremely",
            "ref": "v-extremely"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " sensitive to sunlight. Whenever I go outside, I have to wear very dark sunglasses."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Ever since I was little, my biggest challenge has been fitting in with people who can see the world clearly. In school, I had a hard time playing games or doing group activities with the other students. Because of my poor eyesight, I was often left behind while my classmates moved on."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Things finally began to improve in Grade 3. That year, I was introduced to my first piece of assistive technology. It’s a screen reader called JAWS (Job Access With Speech). When a website is designed to work with it, the screen reader can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "detect",
            "ref": "v-detect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " everything on the page and read it aloud. That was a game-changer for people like me."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "These days, I depend on VoiceOver. This screen reader is built into every Apple device. Thanks to VoiceOver, I’ve been able to explore many parts of the digital world. I can text and email friends and family, listen to my favourite songs online, shop on Amazon, and edit documents. Without a screen reader, all of that would have been out of reach."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I have benefited greatly from assistive technology. However, I still see room for improvement. Many apps and websites are not designed to work well with screen readers. I hope more developers will become aware of the needs of users like me. The digital world should be a place where everyone can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "belong",
            "ref": "v-belong"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
